  "id": "odor",
  "term": "odor",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, odor refers to a smell stimulus that can evoke incidental emotion, such as pleasant or unpleasant affect. The packet supports that such odor-elicited affect can influence how people evaluate moral situations, with effects that vary by age and type of judgment.",
